    "capital": "Live OK RSI capital model (controllers.generic.modular_spot_core.bag.live_capital_exposure/decision, shared with the controller and recomputed by the verifier for every capital decision), in the live gate order: fewer than max_active_tranches active buys; the slice_quote plan, first resized (live V2 funding, when funded_cap_quote is set) to (funded_cap_quote - max(0, net cash spent, inventory cost)) / (1 + funding_fee_reserve), at cost; then held bag (non-dust) plus active buys marked at the bar close plus the buy must stay within position_cap_quote when one is set (absent: no position cap). Without funding (V1) a buy the wallet cannot pay for is refused (live balance_low), wallet cash being equity minus inventory at mark (realized PnL is reinvested). With funding (V2) the buy never exceeds wallet cash net of the round-trip cost reserve (the research wallet, research.wallet_quote or the pair allocation, stays 1x cash); the live V2 strategy-wide allocation (2500 across pairs) is not modelled for this single pair, and funding cost is per lot where live blends one running average. The verifier re-derives every decision's active tranches, held bag, exposure, cash and funded used from the ledgers. Not modelled: dynamic signal-strength sizing (live dynamic_position_sizing, V2 0.5-1.0x, V1 0.5-1.25x; every buy plans the full slice_quote); the live buy-threshold shifts by HMM regime (+-3) and by trend confirmation (down trend: -0.4 x boost x confidence, floor 20); the adaptive (ATR-scaled 45-90 s) and consecutive-loss cooldowns (the sealed acquisition.cooldown_seconds applies instead) and the flash-crash pause unless research.flash_crash. The live scout/runner split is disabled in live (buy_confirmation_mode none). Replaces the fixed-allocation-at-cost entry capital of plain bag mode. research.depth_budget (a research setting, not live OK RSI) then refuses a buy when the bag at cost plus active buys at their quote plus the buy would exceed wallet x min(1, base_fraction + (1 - base_fraction) x depth / full_depth), depth being the price's drawdown below the higher of the highest closed-candle high over lookback_minutes and the held (non-dust) bag's breakeven; the verifier recomputes the recent high from the bars, the breakeven and deployed quote from the ledgers and the decision with the native function.",
